{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6553303","formula":"C₁₁H₁₆BrNO₂","hill":"C11H16BrNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":16.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Meta-DOB"},"descriptions":{"en":"Meta-DOB, also known as 5-bromo-2,4-dimethoxyamphetamine, is a psychoactive drug of the phenethylamine and amphetamine families related to the psychedelic drug DOB. It is a positional isomer of DOB in which the bromine atom at the 4 position and the methoxy group at the 5 position have been interchanged. In his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved), Alexander Shulgin lists meta-DOB's dose range as 50 to 100 mg orally and its duration as 5 to 6 hours."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":143750,"mass":274.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC(=C(C=C1OC)OC)Br)N","inchikey":"YFSLPSITQIUFQK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(5-bromo-2,4-dimethoxyphenyl)propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"143750","atoms":31,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.435,"y":2.767,"z":-0.411,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.822,"y":-2.274,"z":0.332,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.339,"y":-0.01,"z":0.686,"el":"O"},{"x":4.346,"y":1.041,"z":-0.401,"el":"N"},{"x":2.129,"y":0.038,"z":-0.722,"el":"C"},{"x":2.956,"y":1.073,"z":0.063,"el":"C"},{"x":0.667,"y":0.021,"z":-0.343,"el":"C"},{"x":0.092,"y":-1.136,"z":0.162,"el":"C"},{"x":2.945,"y":0.81,"z":1.569,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.078,"y":1.178,"z":-0.514,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.26,"y":-1.135,"z":0.505,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.43,"y":1.178,"z":-0.171,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.021,"y":0.021,"z":0.339,"el":"C"},{"x":0.871,"y":-3.182,"z":-0.766,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.266,"y":-0.39,"z":-0.328,"el":"C"},{"x":2.589,"y":-0.949,"z":-0.595,"el":"H"},{"x":2.189,"y":0.253,"z":-1.798,"el":"H"},{"x":2.574,"y":2.084,"z":-0.114,"el":"H"},{"x":3.594,"y":1.522,"z":2.094,"el":"H"},{"x":3.296,"y"